Hi,
   we have a problem concerning a 4mm DAT cartridge. The tape was used for
backups from a VAX 3100 station with an HP35480A drive. During a recent
backup session we accidentally gave BACKUP/REWIND and thus overwrote
part of our first saveset on this tape. We now want to recover the rest
of the data (the rest of the first saveset and two other ones). We
already tried out several methods to read this data (BACKUP command on
the VAX, FORTRAN program to directly read data from a magnetic tape,
mounting the tape on UNIX machines (SUN & HP) with mt and reading with
dd or read/scanf from C programs). However, all of these failed when
trying to skip the EOT mark.
   Thus our question: has anybody ever faced the same problem ? Is there
any possibilty to recover these data by simple means or does one need
special hardware/software equipment to solve this problem ?

Any comments are appreciated.

Replies to comp.os.vms, comp.sys.vms or as PM to
p633dim@mpirbn.mpifr-bonn.mpg.de.

Thanks in advance.

Dirk


